---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Code from '@popug/design/Code.astro';
import Terminal from '@popug/design/Terminal.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Authentication" description="API tokens, scopes and how to authenticate requests." current="/authentication/">
  <h1>Authentication</h1>
  <p class="lede">All requests to the API and to Storage are authenticated with API tokens.</p>

  <h2>API tokens</h2>
  <p>Create tokens in the Console or with the CLI. Send the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header using the Bearer scheme:</p>
  <Code label="HTTP"><span class="k">Authorization:</span> Bearer pc_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</Code>
  <p>Tokens are shown once when created. Store them in a secrets manager and rotate them regularly.</p>

  <h2>Scopes</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Allows</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>storage:read</code></td><td>List buckets, read and list objects</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>storage:write</code></td><td>Create buckets, upload and delete objects</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>cdn:purge</code></td><td>Purge cached objects</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>admin</code></td><td>Manage tokens and account settings</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Create a token with the CLI</h2>
  <Terminal>popug token create --name ci --scope storage:write --scope cdn:purge</Terminal>

  <h2>Authentication errors</h2>
  <p>Requests without a valid token receive <code>401 Unauthorized</code>:</p>
  <Code label="JSON">{`{
  "error": {
    "code": "unauthorized",
    "message": "Missing or invalid API token."
  }
}`}</Code>
</DocsLayout>
